{"id": "EUVD-2026-59153", "enisaUuid": "31cc466c-df35-384a-8e28-be1a2054a6eb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: nft_fib: reject fib expression on the netdev egress hook\n\nA fib expression in a netdev egress base chain dereferences nft_in(pkt),\nNULL on the transmit path, causing a NULL pointer dereference at eval.\nnft_fib_validate() masks the hook with NF_INET_* values, but netdev hook\nnumbers are a separate enum that aliases them (NF_NETDEV_EGRESS ==\nNF_INET_LOCAL_IN), so an egress chain passes validation and then faults.\n\nAdd nft_fib_netdev_validate() that limits each result/flag to the netdev\nhook where the device it reads exists: the input-device cases (OIF,\nOIFNAME, ADDRTYPE with F_IIF) to ingress, the output-device case (ADDRTYPE\nwith F_OIF) to egress, ADDRTYPE with no device flag to both. Also restrict\nnft_fib_validate() to NFPROTO_IPV4/IPV6/INET so its NF_INET_* masks are\nnot applied to another family's hooks.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:54:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:13", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4fee43759b489559a491f7c95f9bfa7a1d0c7a10", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/568931f26af4727a51e8521f72efbc78d3b82410", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d01c913febead04a01a5f3a6374d1f45504dc523", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f68305267ebda7e839b5e8f77e8d77535a3d5a0f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d07955dd34ecae17d35d8c7d0a273a3fba653a8c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f5p7-25h5-xxwh", "CVE-2026-72254"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.61, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03d4b5d2-dd4c-352f-97db-102c986f0ca9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "42df6e1d221dddc0f2acf2be37e68d553ad65f96 <d07955dd34ecae17d35d8c7d0a273a3fba653a8c"}, {"id": "09486023-1d97-33a0-bb8c-2db360c6db97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.16"}, {"id": "57daf7a1-3e89-35a3-8baf-474ea2f9bb42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.148"}, {"id": "78288cbf-f4a3-3839-9d7b-41d735ed76d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.42"}, {"id": "8eebbe6c-5597-3f21-84f1-7de4f9ce969b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "ae2da060-a915-3606-a9af-4c66e70e445e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "42df6e1d221dddc0f2acf2be37e68d553ad65f96 <f68305267ebda7e839b5e8f77e8d77535a3d5a0f"}, {"id": "c208dd29-4bf6-3a5c-9bd0-6120b5d17fc7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.101"}, {"id": "c20eb08f-8b2c-3e8c-ba98-851d8e4e8ac9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "ca20df97-813c-31a6-a4dc-690184c9c721", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "42df6e1d221dddc0f2acf2be37e68d553ad65f96 <d01c913febead04a01a5f3a6374d1f45504dc523"}, {"id": "cc13dc48-c384-3206-809a-05525d03f8a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "42df6e1d221dddc0f2acf2be37e68d553ad65f96 <4fee43759b489559a491f7c95f9bfa7a1d0c7a10"}, {"id": "cc5c09da-8808-318c-8686-345ff23c656b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "42df6e1d221dddc0f2acf2be37e68d553ad65f96 <568931f26af4727a51e8521f72efbc78d3b82410"}, {"id": "e0324c69-f3d7-3388-94f3-6c6052f98b5c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "79cc5b4a-7f1a-31d7-b1d8-1560fb13fa1e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}